   "quote": "rbs3 TCACACAGGACGGCCGGATG",
   "where": "Online methods, Construction and tuning of repressor expression"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/kaf7c8f5fc10ae23f",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "the range of P is inserted into the PhlF response function, yielding outputs of 16 and 0.1 REU",
   "where": "Results, modelling the NAND circuit"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k6720ddd5e3b828b2",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "the range of P is inserted into the PhlF response function, yielding outputs of 16 and 0.1 REU",
   "where": "Results, modelling the NAND circuit"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k70552c98efe3cd30",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "the range of the P input is converted to 61 and 1.4 REU by the LmrA response function",
   "where": "Results, modelling the NAND circuit"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k3bdf2ca8dbc4a0ad",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "the output of P connected to the QacR gate is 20 and 0.4",
   "where": "Results, modelling the AND circuit"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k44e3bc5dcc1022b4",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "The thresholds for the gates are similar with an average of = 0.4 REU and a range of 0.1 (TarA) to 1.3 REU (ButR).",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/ke99ba415f17d4632",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "The dynamic ranges of the gates vary from 207-fold (SrpR) to 5-fold (SmcR and ButR)",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k73fe83ddc44440bc",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "The final non-toxic induction point occurs at 200, 150, 100, 70, 70, and 70 uM IPTG for ButR, TarA, HapR, ScbR, SmcR, and Orf2, respectively.",
   "where": "Online methods, Cellular growth and toxicity data"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k1802e469360b7571",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "The thresholds for the gates are similar with an average of = 0.4 REU and a range of 0.1 (TarA) to 1.3 REU (ButR).",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/kc8afe613ea00f3c0",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "Five of the repressors yield gates with > 3, with the largest being 6.1 for Orf2.",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k90ee49ca6dd9c8d2",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "all of the NOT gates have sufficiently high ON states (between 3 and 70 REU) to achieve full repression by crossing the threshold required by a downstream circuit",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k2cb632af4fa5fa2c",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "the OFF states range between 0.1 and 2.1 REU",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k3303cc97adc9cc5e",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "The thresholds for the gates are similar with an average of = 0.4 REU",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k7f0eb76fc4fcd759",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1038/nchembio.1411",
   "quote": "with an average induction of 51.3-fold",
   "where": "Results, NOT gate construction & response function measurement"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k63e3328716e59cf4",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1186/1754-1611-3-4",
   "quote": "the reference standard promoter J23101, which has a relative activity of 1 RPU",
   "where": "Discussion"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/kf873df238e9e691a",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1186/1754-1611-3-4",
   "quote": "has an estimated absolute activity of ~0.03 PoPS under specific conditions",
   "where": "Discussion"
  },
  {
   "@id": "delphi:evidence/k970f72619fdc60dd",
   "delphi:kind": "doi",
   "dct:identifier": "10.1186/1754-1611-3-4",
   "quote": "we determined the coefficients of variation of the measured promoter activities across all labs to be 17.2%, 17.1%, and 8.5% for BBa_J23150, BBa_J23151, and BBa_J23101, respectively",
   "where": "Results, multi-laboratory test"
  },
  {
